<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēbēthos</span></b> , i,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small stream in Campania</i>, now <i>Maddalona</i>, on which lay Neapolis, <i><span class="en">Stat. S.
				1, 2, 263</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēbēthis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Sebethos</i>, <i>Sebethian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nympha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 734</span></i>
			: lympha, Col. poët. 10, 134.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
